      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lupton%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "That same year, Lupton became the first Arizona stop for the Santa Fe Railroad, cementing its role in rail history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historic66az.com/lupton/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s early growth was fueled by Route 66, spawning several gas stations and stores that now form its historic core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historic66az.com/lupton/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Archaeological evidence shows human activity in the Lupton area for at least ten thousand years, long before European arrival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
